        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Columbia%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1886 the village boasted 100 houses, a hotel, a store, a post office, a train station, a boat shop, and about 350 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Columbia%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1889 White Deer Township hired its first constable, Moses Brown, who also worked as a shoemaker.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Columbia%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1890s saw New Columbia host a baker, confectioner, ice‑cream shop, and bicycle shop, reflecting its growing local economy.",
